        <body>
            <div xml:id="d338">

                <pb facs="0643" n="1297" sameAs="frus:frus1875v02/pg1297"/>

                <head>No. 630.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Goodenow to Mr. Fish.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Constantinople</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1875-05-07"><hi rendition="#italic">May</hi> 7, 1875</date>.
                        (Received June 1.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 4.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Herewith T have the honor to transmit a
                    copy of a communication addressed to Mr. Boker by the American missionaries and
                    teachers in Robert College, residing here, just before his departure from
                    Constantinople. Mr. Boker expressed his acknowledgments to the deputation who
                    presented the communication in suitable terms.</p>
                <p>As an evidence of the very high esteem in which Mr. Boker was held by his
                    colleagues, as well as by the public in Constantinople, I may mention the fact
                    that the English, French, Russian, and Austrian ambassadors and the Persian
                    minister took leave of him on board the steamer.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>J. H. GOODENOW.</signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d338-a1.xml" xpointer="d338-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
